# Normalise line endings for text, but never touch binaries.
#
# `eol=lf` is not redundant with `text=auto`. text=auto normalises to LF in the
# OBJECT STORE; checkout still follows core.eol, which defaults to native -- so
# a Windows clone gets CRLF working files against LF blobs, and `git status`
# shows nothing because it compares normalised. That drift is invisible until a
# tool writes LF into a CRLF file.
*                text=auto eol=lf

*.png            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.jpeg           binary
*.webp           binary
*.gif            binary
*.pdf            binary
*.zip            binary
*.ttf            binary
*.otf            binary

# The two exceptions that genuinely need CRLF: Windows batch files break without it.
*.bat            text eol=crlf
*.cmd            text eol=crlf

*.sh             text eol=lf
